WEBVTT

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.490
It was not found at the crash site.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.990
Spill it! Where did you hide the relic?

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:25.420
ID... GI187D390...

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.290
Lieutenant Shin Kudou...

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:29.710
Shin!

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:41.470
ID... GI1...

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:46.350
...87D390...

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.050
You dog of the UN.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.360
Stop!

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.370
Then will you tell us where it is?

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.200
Don't touch Sara...

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.630
Under the name of the UN...

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.130
What have you guys done to the women and children?!

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:20.510
Who were the ones who tortured and killed my
parents, and then raped my little sister?

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:23.220
Not me...

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.640
No, it was you.

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:29.730
It was you UN soldiers.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:32.650
And you gave me this scar.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.160
Here.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:43.320
I've brought another one.

00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:12.190
It's already been 30 minutes since the rescue
signal from the missing people disappeared.

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:12.980
We don't have any time to waste!

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.690
Hurry up and hand over the gun pod!

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:21.690
Major, launching the gun pod during refueling
is strictly forbidden in the manual.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.200
You're going to die early if you stick to the manual too much!

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:38.790
That's...

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:50.520
Die.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:58.320
Make it in time!

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.420
Ivanov!

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:16.830
You treat your machine quite roughly, like before.

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:19.050
I've told you...

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:22.930
...to treat them delicately, as if they were a virgin or a feather.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:27.930
It makes me sick when I think that, thanks
to you, I'm the person I am today.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:40.950
You're...

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:42.950
Professor Hasford!

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:49.540
Sara Nome... You've grown.

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:53.950
Professor, why are you with the Anti-UN Alliance?

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:57.630
Who told you to speak?!

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:02.670
Captain Nora, do not hurt them.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:06.640
Remove their restraints.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:24.110
Aries, do you understand why I chose this
as the place where we would be reunited?

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:27.440
Sara probably knows why.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:43.750
This is...

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:47.050
A traditional Mayan wall painting.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:49.140
And there are so many of them!

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.440
Amazing... This is amazing.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:57.680
It's perfect!

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:04.610
The birdman who created the
humans on the Mayan island...

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:09.530
was ordered to sing the song of destruction
by the god of the heavens, Procacha.

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:13.830
When the birdman was told to
do that, he cut off his own head...

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.170
to prevent the song from being sung.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:22.800
But every time a bond between the people
and the Earth is broken...

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:30.680
...it's believed that the head and body move closer together
and will one day sing the song of destruction.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:35.180
Sara.

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:39.060
You were the one who told me that, remember?

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:44.780
You broke that rule to tell me that, Sara.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:05:59.330
You've improved, fledgling.

00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:01.960
I'm happy to see improvement as your instructor.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:07.800
Also, you shared the blood of the family of the priestesses...

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:15.060
...even when your father, Ugari, urged you not to.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:16.720
Sara...

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:22.570
Do you want these again? I still have a lot of them.

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:24.730
No...

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:44.050
You supplied the blood?

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:01.100
No!

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:09.110
This can't be...

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:12.110
The birdman's head is coming!

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:21.120
Something bothersome has come...

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:23.330
Damn it!

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:36.510
What is that?

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:42.020
I taught you to not look away.

00:07:43.360 --> 00:07:44.900
The main engine...

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:47.530
This will end it all.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:08.130
Don't let him get away!

00:08:12.510 --> 00:08:13.630
Sara!

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:27.820
They're not getting away!

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.120
Aries?!

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.670
Focker?

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:52.550
This way!

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.300
Go after the priestess.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:01.560
Bring her back to me, unharmed.

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:05.060
Damn it, you like to give a lot of orders, old geezer.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:42.310
Damn vermin.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.950
Sara, we need to jump!

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:03.860
Sara!

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:49.830
Did you...

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:53.290
Hey!

00:10:56.010 --> 00:10:56.960
Sara!

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:59.380
Hey, wait up.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:03.550
Did that rock fly because of your power?

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:08.940
Why did you help me?

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:11.900
You heard him.

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:14.940
I sinned and broke the rule of blood.

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:17.810
So why did you save me?

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:20.820
Why?!

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:36.420
Do you know where Mao's treasure went?

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:10.000
Can you hear the sound the birdman's
head makes or something like that?

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.460
It's none of your business.

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:23.430
It was a big loss for us to lose the Octos.

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:26.720
Now we have to rappel down the cliffs.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:31.730
If a roach hides beneath your bed,
you just have to destroy the bed.

00:12:32.190 --> 00:12:36.400
If you do that, Hasford will be quite disappointed.

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:40.070
The enemy makes rocks float.

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:41.740
They're equivalent to roaches.

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:45.740
So you're saying they won't die that easily?

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:51.820
Communication officer...

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:54.450
Send an encrypted message to the
Aircraft Carrier <i>Auerstadt</i>...

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.000
Request a fuel-air explosive strike on these coordinates.

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:07.260
The surgery is complete, right?

00:13:07.260 --> 00:13:10.480
Yes... It was a success.

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:12.600
Then why is Mao still asleep?

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.770
Did the white people attach a Kadun to her?

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:21.310
Kinuha...

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.780
We will do the Kinuha ritual.

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:30.790
So, Focker, what are you doing here?

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:35.580
Aren't you supposed to thank me for saving you first?

00:13:35.580 --> 00:13:40.630
My question to you is about this
"What are you doing here?"

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:43.580
Is that the only thing you have to say,
Aries-senpai?

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:49.140
Why don't you shave?

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:51.640
Why do you fly in the sky all the time?

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:56.350
What? Um, that's because...

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:59.060
It's what you call an I-want-to-fly sickness.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:03.140
Why did you go to college if you hated studying?

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:08.690
Why didn't you come that time...?

00:14:13.960 --> 00:14:16.160
That's abrupt.

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.620
That time,

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:24.920
you suddenly said that you were going to be Professor
Hasford's apprentice and headed to Oxford.

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:28.170
<i>Is it my fault?</i>

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:34.220
<i>No, it's my fault for not seeing you off.</i>

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:44.890
<i>If we could have admitted we were wrong back then,
perhaps things could have taken a different course.</i>

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:53.620
There are no "ifs" in history.
I thought that was your specialty.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:56.410
Yeah.

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:01.170
Professor Hasford is with the Anti-UN Alliance.

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.090
It's the ocean!

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:12.140
Don't move! It's a mine!

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:21.850
What is it?

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:26.150
It's the Zero... the Zero Battroid.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:30.900
Is he still alive?

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:40.960
If I had been more cautious...
Wait, there are no "ifs" in history.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:47.340
That's right. Still, I have no intention of
letting your name become history.

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:49.590
Focker...

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:53.090
I'm an ally. Are you okay?

00:15:57.770 --> 00:15:58.760
Don't look.

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:27.340
Does it hurt?

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:35.630
Because I broke the rule of blood,
a lot of blood has been spilled.

00:16:36.470 --> 00:16:38.840
That's just a coincidence.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:44.900
I've broken a lot of rules.

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:53.360
I stole Tom's toy, I broke the vase my mom
treasured and blamed it on my brother...

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:56.110
I also cheated... Wait, you wouldn't understand.

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:59.200
Anyway, it's something you shouldn't do.

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:03.870
I've also stuffed ten frogs into the
bag of a teacher I hated before.

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:12.290
That time, you could hear the teacher scream throughout the school.

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:14.340
What a person you are.

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:17.590
Sara...

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:31.900
Also, I...

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:39.530
I...

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:46.500
You don't have to say it.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:18:01.590
Hey, do you remember China's Liaoning Province?

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:04.430
How can I forget?

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:07.150
Under the burning sun in the desert...

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:10.110
I helped you dig up a fossil of a feathered dinosaur.

00:18:10.690 --> 00:18:13.230
The pay was low, too.

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:18.660
Who was the one who said it'd be
a nice, cheap vacation to China?

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:22.620
Who was the one who went nuts over the fact there
were no separating walls in the bathroom?

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:34.840
But after all the trouble, we finally found one.

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:40.390
Yeah. I thought to myself, even dinosaurs wanted to fly.

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:47.350
Maybe I'm doing what I do because I couldn't
forget the strong impression it made on me.

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:53.860
I thought to myself, humans and all living
things are connected to the past.

00:18:56.150 --> 00:19:01.240
Maybe I'm doing what I do because I couldn't
forget the strong impression it made on me.

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:06.370
Don't move.

00:19:17.180 --> 00:19:20.010
Hey, stop that...

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:23.100
Not at a time like this... If my leg moves...

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:34.940
When did you...

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:39.950
A long time ago.

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:44.200
Geez!

00:20:01.180 --> 00:20:02.000
Sara.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:04.920
Watch out!

00:20:12.360 --> 00:20:14.140
Hurry, grab on.

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:15.690
Sara...

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:17.280
Hurry up and give me your hand.

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:30.000
Be more careful!

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.080
But... it got dark all of the sudden.

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:34.330
Dark?

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:38.170
It's because you've gotten used to electrical light.

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:41.840
But it's useful to have light.

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:43.800
Useful, useful, useful!

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:46.850
You people are always going on about "useful!"

00:20:53.150 --> 00:20:57.180
Mayan people require just the forest and ocean to live.

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:02.860
The ocean and forest listened to Rooy Kanu's wish...

00:21:02.860 --> 00:21:05.690
...and provided us with food and places to live.

00:21:07.330 --> 00:21:10.080
What more do we need?

00:21:12.330 --> 00:21:13.620
That's...

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:17.410
When I was young, my father told me...

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:23.420
...that Mayan and the islands nearby
spoke different languages.

00:21:23.800 --> 00:21:28.970
But as soon as clothes and radios came in,
we eventually spoke one language...

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:31.100
...and we saw things the same way.

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:34.900
In Mayan's old language, it's Kef.

00:21:34.900 --> 00:21:37.230
<i>In Tonan, it's Hao.</i>

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:39.440
<i>In Euclid, it's Kefla.</i>

00:21:40.780 --> 00:21:44.230
<i>But the true name is different.</i>

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:49.740
<i>Rocks, grass, mountains, and everything
else have a true name.</i>

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:58.040
<i>We just forgot those names, and we do not
even attempt to hear the song of truth...</i>

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:01.590
<i>and instead call it "leaf".</i>

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:07.640
I think just having one is okay. Otherwise,
I couldn't talk to you like this.

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:11.550
But in exchange, the word "strife" was introduced.

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:14.100
War came to the island.

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:19.680
And most who leave the island do
not even think of coming back.

00:22:20.530 --> 00:22:22.440
Even if they do come back...

00:22:22.440 --> 00:22:26.110
they say that the island has nothing,
and go back to the cities.

00:22:26.910 --> 00:22:30.620
Everyone likes to refer to going to
the cities as "returning home".

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:36.030
What's so beautiful about those machine lights?

00:22:36.670 --> 00:22:38.620
They merely steal the lights from the sky.

00:22:42.800 --> 00:22:45.170
Maybe you want to go to the cities, too.

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:46.720
No!

00:22:47.470 --> 00:22:50.050
I would never go to the cities!

00:22:50.050 --> 00:22:51.050
Don't force yourself.

00:22:53.140 --> 00:22:54.140
Why do you say that?

00:22:55.310 --> 00:22:58.300
Because you have the same eyes...

00:22:58.900 --> 00:23:03.900
The same eyes as your little sister, Mao... that are pursuing a dream.

00:23:13.990 --> 00:23:14.950
I can hear it...

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:16.450
The enemy?

00:23:16.450 --> 00:23:20.910
I can hear it... The song of one breaking
through armor to create new wings.

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:23.420
What?

00:23:28.680 --> 00:23:29.880
What is it?

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:34.720
Incredible.

00:23:34.720 --> 00:23:38.430
This is a rare luminescent cicada. They are also
known as "the companions of the spirits".

00:25:00.270 --> 00:25:03.060
A new child is going to be born.

00:25:09.860 --> 00:25:11.310
Wow...

00:25:12.780 --> 00:25:14.530
There are so many fireflies.

00:25:15.240 --> 00:25:19.110
Yeah, it looks like the forest is on fire.

00:25:26.340 --> 00:25:29.550
They're singing... a song of life.

00:25:34.010 --> 00:25:35.090
I can hear...

00:25:37.800 --> 00:25:39.260
...the song of the forest.

00:25:39.260 --> 00:25:44.980
The plants and trees of the forest listen to
the birds, animals, and bugs, and grow.

00:25:59.290 --> 00:26:01.700
That's why you were singing...

00:26:05.960 --> 00:26:09.340
...in place of the wounded lives of the forest.

00:26:32.940 --> 00:26:34.020
Shin.

00:26:35.240 --> 00:26:37.320
Are you singing...

00:26:37.320 --> 00:26:41.910
...for the wounded Maya forest? For Mao and its villagers?

00:26:47.750 --> 00:26:50.120
My reason is not that great...

00:26:51.880 --> 00:26:52.670
Sara...

00:26:54.090 --> 00:26:57.220
I'm doing it for someone who is hurt, but
no one has bothered to heal...

00:26:57.220 --> 00:26:58.130
For you.

00:27:25.540 --> 00:27:26.450
Sara.

00:27:55.230 --> 00:27:58.490
A new child was born in the village.

00:27:58.820 --> 00:28:01.990
A child who is stronger than a Kadun.

00:28:10.500 --> 00:28:13.450
It's coming... A Kadun...

00:28:13.920 --> 00:28:16.250
And it's carrying a dreadful flame!

00:29:19.230 --> 00:29:24.910
Chapter Four

00:29:19.230 --> 00:29:24.910
Jungle
